WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.730
Don't think I could ever
be happy without you.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.520
Don't go. Don't leave me.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.110
Please.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.610
I'm begging you, Chloé.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.700
Don't leave me all alone!

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.280
Malnomen...
Millie, Theater of Ice and Snow.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.950
Those afflicted by this malady

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:07.500
are trapped in a closed world,
a frozen prison of their own memories.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.670
The endlessly repeating
performance that plays out there

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.970
slowly but surely destroys their soul.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.600
This malnomen is so intractable

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.140
because you cannot treat it simply
by performing an inverse operation.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.100
Unless the curse-bearer themself
rejects their frozen world,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.650
they will remain bound fast
there until it vanishes,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.530
erasing them from existence.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.110
Chloé d'Apchier!

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:42.450
You can vanish along with this world
or continue to live your dismal life.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.870
Your choice!

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:49.120
Even if you survive this,
you won't reclaim your good name.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.210
The Church will never
admit the truth about the past

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.630
and will keep hunting you as the Beast.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.460
That's enough!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.340
It will be hell either way!

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.300
But you must choose!

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.560
Jean-Jacques?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.480
What have...

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.730
What have I done?

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.620
Jeanne, go!

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.710
If only I could turn back time.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:38.470
If only I hadn't hesitated
to reach out and save you.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.260
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:25.030
Roland, I may soon do harm
to one of your brethren.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.990
Do you speak of the one known as Astolfo?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.500
I see.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.960
He is up there now.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.040
Astolfo's entire family
was slain by vampires.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.460
Enough!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.050
I'm sorry.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.680
I won't tell you not to fight him.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.510
I'm not sure why I told you this.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.350
I suppose I simply wanted you to know.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.560
That young lad was far too kind.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.150
Die!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.610
All vampires must die!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.200
He has injected far too much!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.370
Please stop this, Captain!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.250
Your body cannot withstand any more!

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.000
Oh no! He's got me this time!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.760
Now what?! Should I fall back?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.600
Do not hesitate, Noé.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:34.020
Do not consider whether
Astolfo's hatred is justified.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:39.060
Humans and vampires alike act according
to their own sense of what's right.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.650
One man's justice can be another's evil.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.610
In your case, right makes might.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:51.620
But such might can easily turn to
a violence more vexing than malice.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.660
Do not wield it in anger.
Keep it deep inside.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:06:01.210
Let that sense of justice be a shining
light guiding you on your path.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.340
That means don't overthink it!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:15.100
Act according to where you draw the line,
not what you feel is right.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.690
That will serve you well
at the very least.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.070
I will not retreat, no matter what!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.570
I'll blow you to bits!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.000
I want to save Chloé and Jean-Jacques.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.420
That's all I want, no matter who's my foe!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.680
I'll never give up!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.520
Nice one!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.860
Young Master! Dear Astolfo!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:16.830
I wanted to be human again,

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:21.500
for that is what Father wished.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.130
Father dedicated his life

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:30.050
to researching how to
return me to human form.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.890
That was a joy to me.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:38.430
It was all an expression
of his love for me, and...

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.270
...it was a lie.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.770
The truth is, I was always lonely.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:52.570
After all, if I was not human,
it meant I was not truly me.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:57.200
The engine is at its limit!
It can't sustain her existence!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.830
There's no time for an inverse operation!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.210
I wanted to be accepted

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.380
as a daughter to her father,

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.420
as a member of the d'Apchier family,

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.840
as I truly am.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.560
Chloé!

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.930
I wanted to be loved

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.230
for who I truly am.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.150
You must choose!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.410
Damn it!

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.580
Luna, lend me your strength.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.570
It looks like the heavens
are blue and filled with stars.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.710
Now I see. That is your true name.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:30.880
Canorus, "she who makes
music with snow flowers."

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.730
What happened? It's no longer cold.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.490
Snow?

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.990
No, they're flower petals.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:05.700
Does this mean it's over?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:09.170
Well done, you two.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.820
Huh? Ow... Ouch!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.280
The pain is way worse than
I thought! Like 15 times worse!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.160
Hey, I found it! I found your hand!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.830
Are you all right?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.540
No. I think I shall cry.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.960
You think we can reattach it?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.840
Well, it's not like it
got burned to ashes.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.340
It might work... or not. I have no idea.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:07.100
Where did all those
astérisque flowers come from?

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.770
Haven't you heard?

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:11.270
They're said to bloom in and around areas

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.060
where the World Formula
has been tampered with.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.780
But I don't know if it's true.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.950
You've got to be kidding me!

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.540
Kill...

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:33.290
I must kill every last vampire.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.170
I must kill them.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.000
Astolfo.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.210
H-Help us.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:22.590
Please... Sir Paladin.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.590
I beg you.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:29.100
Please save my sister.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.730
I don't care what happens to me.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:39.730
I'm to blame. This is all...

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.240
...my fault.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:50.120
It's over now, Astolfo.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.200
Come with me.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:58.420
Captain. Young Master Astolfo.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.810
Chloé! Are you all right?!

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.400
How do you feel? Is anything wrong?

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.820
Chloé!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:28.280
You fool! I never said you could
get so battered and bruised!

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.950
What if you had gotten yourself killed?!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.700
What?! I could say the same about you!

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.620
You planned to die
without even telling me!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.710
Did you ever consider how
I'd feel being left all alone?!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.510
That's enough!
How dare you talk back to me!

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.420
I hate you, Jean-Jacques!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.340
Chloé.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.720
You fool. You fool!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.800
You utter fool!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.060
Chloé?!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.060
I vowed not to cry.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:44.270
When I decided to exact
vengeance upon that nightmare,

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.820
I vowed I would no longer cry, but...

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.910
I'm such a fool, aren't I?

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:53.490
Jeanne, that day I gazed up
at the sky with you...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:58.790
I truly thought that if I were to die,
I'd like it to be that day.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.920
But now...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.840
I want to live.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.300
That is what I now wish.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:16.720
Wasn't that unfair of me?
Haven't I been awful?

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:25.110
What's wrong with that?
I don't mind if you're unfair.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:29.490
Let's both live, Chloé, together.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:36.490
I don't need anything more
than you being there for me.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.590
Vanitas.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.340
Where is he?!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.230
It's spread quite a bit.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.240
It's so cold.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:16.700
Vanitas!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.990
Jeanne!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.700
You're all right?

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:24.120
Thank you, Vanitas! Thank you!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.090
Chloé's survived! You really saved her!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.460
Thank you!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:32.010
O-Ow! It's a little early
to take a victory lap.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.510
I don't know what
Lord Ruthven is really up to.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.640
But I doubt the Senate
will let Chloé d'Apchier be.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:42.270
And you'll likely suffer
some sort of punishment.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.020
I'm well aware of that!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:47.190
But I'm still happy! Hopelessly so!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.070
Okay...

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.530
How could I help it?!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:50.990
My bad.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:54.570
Vanitas, thanks to you...

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.200
Because you were there for me...

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.740
I...

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:19.430
Wait, Jeanne! What's gotten into you?

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:43.830
I-I did offer my blood to you.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:48.210
But there is a time and
a place for everything.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:11.230
Remember your promise, Vanitas.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.690
If the day ever comes

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:17.490
when I am truly no longer myself...

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.370
If that were to happen,

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.380
you must slay me, understand?

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.140
Jeanne!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.200
Listen to me.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.080
Everyone is alone.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:15.050
That doesn't change whether
you are a human or a vampire.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:19.050
You can never completely
understand someone.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:25.640
Most people live and die without
even understanding themselves.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.060
Nevertheless, it is for that very reason

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:33.810
people seek each other out to share
the warmth of an emotional bond.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:42.450
Someday, when I no longer walk this earth,

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:48.160
may you find someone to
snuggle up with just as we are now.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:53.290
Or should I say, I'm sure
there will be such a person...

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:58.210
...as long as you do not close your heart.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:08.310
Open your heart, and you will never
be lonely even when you are alone,

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:14.020
just as both of you are here for me.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.860
Vanitas!

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.280
Um, are you all right?

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.450
Huh?

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.280
You always complained about the cold,

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:31.580
but I know one day, you will meet
someone who will keep you warm.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.840
Are you sure about this?

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:45.300
Yes. I always wanted
the strength to protect Chloé.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:50.350
But if it's just going to do her harm,

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.020
I no longer need it.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.440
I myself must be enough.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:01.490
I, Jean-Jacques Chastel,
shall protect her!

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.950
Very well.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:25.180
Yes, your true name suits you well.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:33.350
Aprix, "he who nestles up
to the last snows."

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:44.450
So it was that Gévaudan was
finally freed from the Beast's curse.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.740
Some were saved.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.080
And some were not.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.160
That's it!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:56.540
But the scars will
remain on each one of us.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:05.010
"Snow Flower"

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:41.500
"The Incurable Disease"
